# The rows of src/runtime/recipes/vulpen/library/parts/projects/Projects.cpp, a call each (src/tools/bench/bench.py).

## Projects.cpp/Projects::bind
command view list projects: lists the projects, by their folders from the projects' folder, whose names view load takes
command view load <project>: hosts the view of a project by name, or of a folder by path from where vulpen started, or of the one folder in it holding a view, as a repository's; an app's name, as ide, hosts the app beside the projects again
command view new [<project>]: hosts a new, empty view, a project's by name or a folder's by path from where vulpen started, with none project1 on, the first free, and saves its view.vlp
command view remove <project>: closes a project, if it is hosted, and deletes its folder with all it holds, as node remove does a node's
command view rename <name>: saves the view, renames its folder where it is, and hosts it under the new name
command view save as [<name>]: copies the view, its edits too, into a new project, with no name the view's numbered on, as wave2, and works on the copy; the view's own files stay as last saved

## Projects.cpp/Projects::folder_of
a path elsewhere -> sent [": view add mine <here>/elsewhere/mine/view.vlp", "mine: view save", "view switch mine"]; answered ["made <here>/elsewhere/mine/view.vlp; lines go to mine now"]
a path named triangle elsewhere -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "<here>/projects/triangles/triangle holds a project named triangle already, and the build holds one view of each name"
a path to a view.vlp -> sent [": view add new <here>/new/view.vlp", "new: view save", "view switch new"]; answered ["made <here>/new/view.vlp; lines go to new now"]
a path whose folder is a.b, no project's name -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "a.b cannot be hosted: a view takes its folder's name, and a name holds letters, digits, _ and -"
a path whose folder is c++ -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "c++ cannot be hosted: a view takes its folder's name, and a name holds letters, digits, _ and -"
a path whose folder is my proj -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "my proj cannot be hosted: a view takes its folder's name, and a name holds letters, digits, _ and -"
empty, a folder holding none -> sent [": view add empty <here>/projects/empty/view.vlp", "empty: view save", "view switch empty"]; answered ["made <here>/projects/empty/view.vlp; lines go to empty now"]
fresh -> sent [": view add fresh <here>/projects/fresh/view.vlp", "fresh: view save", "view switch fresh"]; answered ["made <here>/projects/fresh/view.vlp; lines go to fresh now"]
fresh, a view hosted under that name -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "a view named fresh is hosted already, from <here>/elsewhere/fresh/view.vlp"
triangle, a group's -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "<here>/projects/triangles/triangle holds a view already; view load hosts it"
wave, a view there -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "<here>/projects/wave holds a view already; view load hosts it"

## Projects.cpp/Projects::free_project
none -> sent [": view add project1 <here>/projects/project1/view.vlp", "project1: view save", "view switch project1"]; answered ["made <here>/projects/project1/view.vlp; lines go to project1 now"]
none, project1 a folder, project2 hosted, project3 a group's -> sent [": view add project4 <here>/projects/project4/view.vlp", "project4: view save", "view switch project4"]; answered ["made <here>/projects/project4/view.vlp; lines go to project4 now"]

## Projects.cpp/Projects::host
a b, no name -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "a b is no project's name, which is letters, digits, _ and -; a path to a folder holds a /"
cli, an app -> sent [": view add cli <here>/recipes/cli/view.vlp"]; answered ["loaded the app cli beside the projects"]
cli, hosted already -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "a view named cli is hosted already, from <here>/recipes/cli/view.vlp"
empty, holding none -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "<here>/projects/empty holds no view.vlp; view new starts a view there"
gone, no folder -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "<here>/projects/gone holds no view.vlp; view new starts a view there"
ide, the app vulpen started with -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "ide is the view vulpen started with, which runs already"
repo, whose one folder holds a view -> sent [": view add inner <here>/projects/repo/inner/view.vlp", "view switch inner"]; answered ["loaded <here>/projects/repo/inner/view.vlp; lines go to inner now"]
the path of wave's folder -> sent [": view add wave <here>/projects/wave/view.vlp", "view switch wave"]; answered ["loaded <here>/projects/wave/view.vlp; lines go to wave now"]
the path of wave's folder, a / after it -> sent [": view add wave <here>/projects/wave/view.vlp", "view switch wave"]; answered ["loaded <here>/projects/wave/view.vlp; lines go to wave now"]
the path of wave's view.vlp -> sent [": view add wave <here>/projects/wave/view.vlp", "view switch wave"]; answered ["loaded <here>/projects/wave/view.vlp; lines go to wave now"]
the projects' folder by its path -> sent [": view add wave <here>/projects/wave/view.vlp", "view switch wave"]; answered ["loaded <here>/projects/wave/view.vlp; lines go to wave now"]
triangle-params, in a group -> sent [": view add triangle-params <here>/projects/triangles/triangle-params/view.vlp", "view switch triangle-params"]; answered ["loaded <here>/projects/triangles/triangle-params/view.vlp; lines go to triangle-params now"]
two, whose two folders hold a view each -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "<here>/projects/two holds no view.vlp, and 2 folders in it do: a, b; view load takes the path of one"
wave -> sent [": view add wave <here>/projects/wave/view.vlp", "view switch wave"]; answered ["loaded <here>/projects/wave/view.vlp; lines go to wave now"]
wave, a view of that name hosted from elsewhere -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "a view named wave is hosted already, from <here>/elsewhere/view.vlp"
wave, hosted from its folder -> sent ["view switch wave"]; answered ["wave is loaded already; lines go to it now"]

## Projects.cpp/Projects::projects
a file beside them, and a view two folders down -> sent []; answered ["repo/inner", "triangles/triangle-params", "triangles/triangle", "two/a", "two/b", "wave"]
the tree -> sent []; answered ["repo/inner", "triangles/triangle-params", "triangles/triangle", "two/a", "two/b", "wave"]

## Projects.cpp/Projects::remove
a path -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "<here>/projects/wave is no project's name, which is letters, digits, _ and -, as view list shows it; view remove takes no path"
empty, holding no view -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "no project is named empty: <here>/projects/empty holds no view.vlp"
gone -> sent []; throws runtime_error: "no project is named gone: <here>/projects/gone holds no view.vlp"
triangle, a group's -> sent ["remove force <here>/projects/triangles/triangle/"]; answered ["removed"]
wave, a view of that name hosted from elsewhere -> sent ["remove force <here>/projects/wave/"]; answered ["removed"]
wave, hosted -> sent [": view close force wave", "remove force <here>/projects/wave/"]; answered ["removed"]
wave, not hosted -> sent ["remove force <here>/projects/wave/"]; answered ["removed"]

